{"abstract":[{"text":"Derive an event’s conformances, name and schema from its struct declaration, and declare the constraints its properties satisfy.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" makes a struct an event. It adds the "},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"BinaryCodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformances, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s name, consent category and schema version when you give them, a "},{"code":"schema","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" describing each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stored property in declaration order, and an encoding that writes each stored property under its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name. "},{"code":"@Constrained","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" declares rules a plain "},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", number or array can’t carry, such as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minimum length or a pattern; the macro checks each keyword as it expands, and a tracker rejects an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event whose property breaks one."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" includes this module. It re-exports "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Events"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Persistence"},{"type":"text","text":", so a file that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"imports "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventMacros"},{"type":"text","text":" alone can expand the macro too. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryCodable"},{"type":"text","text":" protocols’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"documentation, in those modules, shows the conformances written by hand. To export the schemas as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a JSON Schema tracking plan, pass them to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlans"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import EventMacros","","@Event(name: \"search_performed\", consent: .functional, version: 2)","struct SearchPerformed {","    @Constrained(.minLength(1), .maxLength(200))","    var query: String","    var resultCount: Int","    var filter: String?","}","","let names = SearchPerformed.schema.properties.map(\\.name)  \/\/ [\"query\", \"resultCount\", \"filter\"]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Raise ","type":"text"},{"code":"version:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only for a change that records stored at the earlier version can’t be read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through; a store drops those records rather than reading them as the new shape.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers both macros, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shows which changes need a new version."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros\/Event(name:consent:version:)"],"title":"Defining an event","anchor":"Defining-an-event"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros\/Constrained(_:)"],"title":"Constraining properties","anchor":"Constraining-